# e2e-tests coverage allowlist — renet functions shipped but not yet exercised
# by a LIVE suite (one CI runs). Read by scripts/gates/check-e2e-coverage.ts through
# the shared BLOCKER contract (scripts/lib/blocker-validator.ts): every entry
# needs a substantive reason, and an entry that BECOMES covered fails the gate
# as stale — so this list can only shrink, never quietly harbor paid-down debt.
#
# This is the forward-direction allowlist ONLY (is every shipped verb tested?).
# The reverse direction (does a test dispatch a verb renet no longer registers?)
# lives in .ci/scripts/quality/check_e2e_coverage.py and has no allowlist.

# BLOCKER: legacy renet functions that predate the packages/e2e-tests suite and
# are not yet exercised by any suite CI runs. The middleware-backed
# packages/cli/tests suite that once covered them was retired; migrating each
# into packages/e2e-tests is tracked follow-up work (the datastore-centric
# redesign wave burns these down — repository_policy_{get,set}/repository_trim
# land in the B4 policy/trim extension, the autostart family and repository_cat/
# diff/ownership/prune/down_all/up_all follow). Remove a name here the moment its
# e2e-test lands; the gate rejects a stale (now-covered) entry automatically.
backup_delete
backup_list
ceph_client_mount
ceph_client_unmount
ceph_clone_image
container_remove
repository_autostart_disable_all
repository_autostart_enable_all
repository_autostart_list
repository_cat
repository_commit_meta
repository_diff
repository_down_all
repository_ownership
repository_prune
repository_template_apply
repository_up_all

# BLOCKER: machine_uninstall tears the renet install off a machine, so exercising
# it means sacrificing the very VM the rest of the suite runs on. No live config
# provisions a throwaway machine for it, and adding one is fleet work this wave
# does not carry.
#
# It was NEVER covered. It only looked covered because the header comment of
# 01-system-checks.test.ts lists the whole setup DOMAIN, and check-e2e-coverage
# counted a verb literal appearing anywhere in a live suite -- comments included.
# Stripping comments from that scan is what surfaced this, so the entry is a
# pre-existing debt made visible rather than a new one.
#
# This entry expires itself: the gate REJECTS an allowlisted name that becomes
# covered, so the day a suite really drives it, this line fails until deleted.
machine_uninstall

